# gen_fu_l58_decrement_saturate.log -- the outstanding counters saturate the DECREMENT, and the two properties
# that read them are one defect (TB Infra, 2026-09-05). Landing 58, feature group "outstanding counters",
# answering rev66's two Mediums and its Lows, and the Critic's L-2, L-4 and L-5.
#
# ================ THE COUNTING RULE, STATED FIRST AND CORRECTED ==========================================
# I have had this wrong twice and rev66 corrected the second version, so it goes at the top with its own
# measurement. Grepping a log for an assertion id and calling the result a firing count is wrong THREE ways.
# On out_l53wrapmut/r, for sva_dbus_outstanding_max, measured rather than reasoned:
#   5285  lines mentioning the id
#   2642  lines that are real UVM_ERRORs (matching '^UVM_ERROR [^:]')
#   2641  the number UVM's own per-id report line carries
# The doubling is the VCS assertion-source line printed beside each UVM_ERROR. The PLUS ONE is the per-id
# report line "[sva_dbus_outstanding_max]  2641" in the Report Summary, NOT the overall tally: the tally reads
# "UVM_ERROR : 2647" and carries no id at all, so it never matches an id-scoped grep. My earlier logs said the
# plus one was the tally. It was not.
# AND UVM'S OWN NUMBER UNDERCOUNTS, which is the third way and the one nobody had named. 2641 firings occur
# before the Report Summary is generated and ONE occurs after it, during the drain, so the per-id line cannot
# see it. Counting from the per-id line would have been wrong by exactly that.
# The rule: count firings with '^UVM_ERROR [^:]' scoped to the id, never lines mentioning the id and never the
# per-id report line.
#
# ================ ROW 1: the DECREMENT saturates, not the sum ============================================
# Landing 55 saturated the SUM: a response was forced to zero when the count plus this cycle's grant was zero.
# rev66 found the residue: a grant and a spurious response in the SAME cycle leave the sum at one, so the test
# never fires, the subtraction still happens, and the count lands one below the truth. One below is permanent.
# The fix subtracts a response only when a beat was outstanding BEFORE this edge:
#   outstanding <= outstanding + ((req && gnt) ? 1 : 0) - ((rvalid && outstanding > 0) ? 1 : 0);
# and the same shape on both counters in the properties file. FOUR CASES TRACED, all against the pre-update
# count: spurious alone, 0 + 0 - 0 = 0, saturated; grant with a spurious response, 0 + 1 - 0 = 1, which is the
# truth and where the sum form gave 0; a normal response, 3 + 0 - 1 = 2; a normal grant, 0 + 1 - 0 = 1.
#
# THE RED. Builds from two archives of 4bd933f: E is that archive unchanged (landing 55's sum form), F is that
# archive with this landing's two tb files. Mutation MUT-SPURIOUSWINDOW, a response asserted with the pending
# queue empty on every cycle from 300 to 399 so that some coincide with grants, on both bus agents. Fixture
# gen_ut_irq on the irq1 program, seed 1.
#   E build_sources_sha256 1c4f99930208695f      F build_sources_sha256 dd9f4cd5ddd825de
#
#   build              rvalid_legal   ibus_rvalid_outstanding   dbus_rvalid_outstanding   real UVM_ERROR
#   E (sum form)           129                  29                        100                  2640
#   F (decrement)          110                  10                        100                  2602
#
# THE READING, and the accounting closes to the digit. The DBUS obligation reads 100 in BOTH: those are the
# injected violations themselves, so the fix loses NO real report, which is the claim that decides the design
# exactly as it did for landing 53. The IBUS obligation drops 29 to 10 and the interface check drops 129 to
# 110, the SAME nineteen, and the totals drop 2640 to 2602, which is 38 = 19 + 19. Nineteen FALSE failures on
# legal traffic removed, every real report kept.
# THIS IS THE HALF LANDING 55 COULD ONLY STATE. Its log named false failures on legal traffic as the second of
# three wrong signals and had no measurement of them. Nineteen of them, and their removal, is that measurement.
# CONTROL: all six smokes PASS on the F build with zero referee errors.
#
# ================ ROW 2: the two properties are ONE defect, not two ======================================
# My landing-55 log says at :27-28 that after one spurious response the counter is "permanently ONE LESS than
# the true outstanding count, and every later update preserves the offset", which is right, and never says that
# one less READS AS 4294967295 when the true count is zero, nor that this is what makes the bound property
# flood. A
# reader can take the bound property and the response obligation for two defects. They are one, seen from the
# two ends of the same counter, and the re-dump shows it as a strict alternation.
# From /proj_soc/user_dev/fzhang/ibex_dv_out/redump_4017573/runs/gen_test_irq_basic_165313640/sim.log, every
# real UVM_ERROR in cycle order with the bound property's runs collapsed:
#   gnt_only_with_req 18334
#   rvalid_outstanding 18345  rvalid_legal 18345  outstanding_max 18346..18354   (9)
#   rvalid_outstanding 18363  rvalid_legal 18363  outstanding_max 18364..18403  (40)
#   rvalid_outstanding 18408  rvalid_legal 18408  outstanding_max 18409..18417   (9)
#   rvalid_outstanding 18422  rvalid_legal 18422  outstanding_max 18423..18449  (27)
#   rvalid_outstanding 18457  rvalid_legal 18457  outstanding_max 18458..18481  (24)
#   rvalid_outstanding 18979  rvalid_legal 18979  outstanding_max 18980..19027  (48)
#   rvalid_outstanding 19032  rvalid_legal 19032  outstanding_max 19033..19103  (71)
#   rvalid_outstanding 19108  rvalid_legal 19108  outstanding_max 19109..19160  (52)
# Eight obligations, eight floods, strict alternation, and the run's last line is inside the eighth flood.
# WHY THAT IS THE OFFSET. One below the truth reads as four billion, so with the true count at zero the bound
# property floods; one grant increments it, four billion plus one is zero, so the bound is satisfied while the
# truth is one, and the next response reads zero and fires. The flood lengths are the intervals in which the
# true count sits at zero.
# IT ALSO ANSWERS AN OBJECTION rather than contradicting it: a counter STUCK at its maximum could not produce
# eight repeats, because the obligation would be satisfied forever. It does not stay there.
# AND AN INDEPENDENT CORROBORATION I DID NOT EXPECT: sva_rvalid_legal fires at the IDENTICAL eight cycles and
# nowhere else. That is the interface counter landing 55 fixed, showing the same offset on the same bus at the
# same instants with no shared code, which is stronger than the equal totals landing 55 rested on.
# NOT CLAIMED: which of the eight are real and which are the offset's own false failures. That needs the
# per-cycle counter value, not the message text.
#
# ================ ROW 3 (rev66 Medium 1): the annotation, and the parameter from the BUILD ================
# The landing-55 annotation named a second route to two data beats. rev66 rejected it and I first "corrected"
# it by citing gen_dut_top.sv:51, WritebackStage = 1'b0. That is a DEFAULT and this build overrides it. From
# the build rather than the source, three ways:
#   compile line       -pvalue+WritebackStage=1
#   elaboration log    assign 1 /gen_tb_top/WritebackStage (global:"command line":0)
#   the DUT's banner   RV32E=0 BranchTargetALU=1 WritebackStage=1 ICache=1 ICacheECC=1 ICacheScramble=1
# So ID takes gen_stall_mem, where data_req_allowed = ~outstanding_memory_access (rtl/ibex_id_stage.sv:1019),
# and no second request issues while one is outstanding. The misaligned split remains the only path to two.
# Same conclusion, different mechanism, and rev66's own premise was the default too. The rule I take from it:
# a parameter declaration gives a default and says nothing about the configuration under test; cite the
# elaboration log, the compile line or the banner beside the source line.
#
# ================ ROW 4 (rev66 Medium 2): the build identity, by base and digest =========================
# The landing-55 log calls its roots "an archive of HEAD", which names no commit and left the saturating
# build's identity unresolvable. For this landing: base 4bd933f, both roots archives of it, and the only files
# copied over F are dv/auto_dv/tb/gen_bus_if.sv and dv/auto_dv/tb/gen_protocol_props.sv as handed with this
# log. Each mutant build differs from its clean sibling in gen_agents_pkg.sv alone, and both roots were
# reverted to the committed agent md5 3690968c afterwards.
#
# ================ ROW 5: the landing-53 A/B figures ======================================================
# gen_fu_l53_outstanding_saturate.log:31-32 prints "3 fires" in both columns and "5285 error lines". Counted
# as firings from the retained runs, out_l53wrapmut/r (build cb66d1b569cba4fb) and out_l53satmut/r
# (0d548320b34bf9d9), both gen_ut_irq seed 1 on the irq1 program:
#   response obligation   1 firing in EACH build          (the log says 3, which is its 3 lines mentioning the id)
#   bound property        2642 wrapping, 0 saturating     (the log says 5285, which is its line count)
# The conclusion is untouched: the response obligation fires the SAME number in both, so saturating loses no
# report, and the bound property goes from many to zero. Only the two integers were wrong.
#
# ================ THE REMAINING ROWS ====================================================================
# rev66, the cover match counts: NOT measured, and said so rather than asserted. The landing-53 log states the
# five covers read zero match in both builds; I have not re-derived those from a vdb and this landing does not.
# rev66, the mutants as prose: answered by landing 57's retention, which puts both mutant diffs under
# dv/auto_dv/evidence/gen_irq_fixtures/ rather than in a log's prose.
# rev66, two overstatements of mine, both corrected here, quoted as they stand rather than tidied. The l55 log
# at :84 says a single injection at cycle 300 leaves "the whole rest of the run is traffic after" it; I had not
# characterised that fixture's traffic and the phrase claims more than I measured. At :94-95 it says the second
# fire corresponds to no "event at all" (the phrase wraps the line there); there WAS an event, a legitimate data
# response, reported falsely. The second is the worse one, because it describes a false report as no report.
# The Critic's L-2: the equality of the two builds' response-obligation counts in landing 53 is a QUIET-FIXTURE
# artefact, not a general property. On that fixture one violation is injected and one is reported either way.
# The claim it supports, that saturating loses no report, is by construction rather than by that measurement,
# and this landing's own red is the general evidence: 100 injected, 100 reported by both forms.
# The Critic's L-4 and L-5 are dispositioned in landing 55's log and its companion and are not reopened here.
